<comment>
problem   = 3D Circularly Polarized Alfvén Wave -- convergence test
reference = G. Toth. JCP, vol. 161, pp. 605-662 (2000)

Box: Lx=3, Ly=Lz=1.5.  Grid: 2N × N × N.
Wave propagates along (1,2,2)/3 (the domain diagonal); one wavelength
per period. With v_A = B_par/sqrt(rho) = 1, the period is T = lambda/v_A = 1.
t_end = 5 corresponds to five complete periods, so the analytic state
returns exactly to the initial condition.

Angles ang_2 and ang_3 are not set here: cpaw.cpp auto-computes them
from the box dimensions, giving n = (1,2,2)/3 for this 3:1.5:1.5 box.

Resolution (nx1,nx2,nx3) and meshblock sizes are meant to be overridden
on the command line. This file contains the smallest supported set.

<job>
problem_id = cpaw

<problem/cpaw>
compute_error = true
b_par   = 1.0     # B parallel (sets Alfven speed = 1 with rho=1)
b_perp  = 0.1     # B perpendicular (perturbation amplitude)
pres    = 0.1     # pressure
v_par   = 0.0     # traveling wave (v_par=0), not standing
dir     = 1       # right polarization

<parthenon/mesh>
refinement = none
nghost = 3

nx1 = 16
x1min = 0.0
x1max = 3.0
ix1_bc = periodic
ox1_bc = periodic

nx2 = 8
x2min = 0.0
x2max = 1.5
ix2_bc = periodic
ox2_bc = periodic

nx3 = 8
x3min = 0.0
x3max = 1.5
ix3_bc = periodic
ox3_bc = periodic

minimum_number_of_teams_for_boundary_kernel = 256

<parthenon/meshblock>
nx1 = 16
nx2 = 8
nx3 = 8

<parthenon/time>
integrator = rk3
cfl = 0.4
tlim = 5.0
nlim = 1000000
perf_cycle_offset = 2

<hydro>
fluid = glmmhd
eos = adiabatic
reconstruction = ppm  
riemann = hlld
gamma = 1.666666666666667
scratch_level = 1
